WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.271
Long before Robert Pattinson signed on the
dotted line to star as Bruce Wayne in The

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.380
Batman, the internet lit up like a Christmas
tree with hot takes on the news.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.600
Now, director Matt Reeves has broken his silence
on the "Battinson" hullabaloo … kind of!

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.340
On June 3rd, Reeves addressed Pattinson's
casting in The Batman in a very 2019 way.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.160
He posted a GIF of Pattinson in 2017's criminally
underrated Good Time, and then added three

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.900
bat emojis for a caption.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:31.199
While Warner Bros. hasn't released an official
statement about Pattinson's involvement as

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.500
of the making of this video, Reeves' simple
tweet basically seals the deal.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.620
The GIF and caption combination gets the message
across perfectly: Pattinson is the new Bruce

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:44.910
Wayne, and Reeves clearly wants fans to be
aware of Pattinson's most critically acclaimed

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:45.960
role to date.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.600
In not overtly praising Pattinson, the filmmaker
didn't stoke the fires burning on the side

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:55.410
of social media that wants to vilify Pattinson
and slam him as a terrible choice to succeed

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.820
Ben Affleck as Batman on the basis that he
starred in the Twilight movies the better

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.340
part of a decade ago.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.420
Reeves did just enough to let his thoughts
be heard without making the situation even

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.460
more divisive than it already is.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.880
When Pattinson's name first sprang up in connection
with The Batman, thousands of people hopped

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.970
on Twitter to shout into the social media
sphere about what they thought of the English

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.640
actor portraying Bruce Wayne.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.080
Many shared that they absolutely hate the
idea, while some were conflicted by the whole

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.100
notion like film critic Mike McGranaghan,
who tweeted,

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.700
"I honestly don't know how to feel about Robert
Pattinson as Batman.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.500
On one hand, I hate the idea, because I can't
even remotely picture him as the Dark Knight.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.500
On the other hand, I absolutely love the idea
for the exact same reason."

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.080
Others held nothing back in denouncing Pattinson
as a poor pick for Batman.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.180
One user wrote,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.180
"I've never been so disappointed in a #Batman
casting, #RobertPattinson is a horrible choice

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.100
to play the character."

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:53.340
Someone else directly called out Reeves and
criticized him for casting Pattinson as the

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.740
new Dark Knight, writing,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.540
"[I've] loved batman films since being a child
and you've completely ruined it for me and

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.860
hundreds of thousands of others by casting
Robert Pattinson as batman, you should check

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.600
the comment sections on pages which have shared
this news, bad move."

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.590
While those individuals were huffing and puffing
over the "Battinson" news, others were firing

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:17.160
shots at the naysayers and defending Warner
Bros. and Reeves' decision to cast Pattinson

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:17.800
as Batman.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.580
An argument many repeated in their pro-Pattinson
tweets involved Heath Ledger's casting as

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.180
the Joker.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.810
When Ledger was confirmed for the Joker, plenty
didn't like the thought of the actor entering

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.990
the DC movie world to play the infamous villain
for the sole reason that he had made a name

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.060
for himself with light-hearted movies like
10 Things I Hate About You.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.880
As we all know, Ledger proved everyone wrong
and his take on the Joker is now a favorite

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.000
amongst fans.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.720
"Why so serious?"

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.860
Many believe the same thing could end up happening
with Pattinson and his performance as Batman.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.580
Like artist Jen Bartel said,

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.040
"Robert Pattinson hasn't been Edward Cullen
since 2012.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.010
Heath Ledger was known for playing teenage
heartthrobs in movies like 10 Things I Hate

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:01.959
About You and A Knight's Tale before he went
on to play what is widely considered the most

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.810
terrifying version of The Joker.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.500
Grow up."

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.900
Some may still be unsure of Pattinson's ability
to knock the Batarang out of the park when

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.130
he dons the cape and cowl in The Batman, but
there are several reasons why he's actually

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:18.150
a flawless fit for the role more so than any
of the dozen or so other actors once rumored

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:19.360
to be in consideration.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.570
"How would you like it if I made you cry,
huh?

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.220
Would you like that?"

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:26.220
He's got the acting chops, the brooding nature
required to play the tortured billionaire

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.959
orphan, and, as Willem Dafoe astutely pointed
out, the strong chin needed to embody Bruce

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:31.460
Wayne.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.780
The Batman is scheduled to fly into theaters
on June 25, 2021.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.380
Then, the world can decide whether Battinson
is better or worse than Battfleck.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:41.880
"Breathe it in.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.160
That's fear!"

